Added `AIModel.default_parameters`, a JSON object of extra request parameters to send with every call to a model. It covers what the two existing columns do not: `seed` for a deterministic run, `reasoning_effort` for a reasoning model, `top_k` and `top_p` for a local model, `extra_body` for a parameter a unified client has no name for, and the two repetition penalties.
Added an allowlist for those keys, checked when a record is saved and again when the parameters are read. An allowlist rather than a denylist, because the keyword surface of a unified LLM client is wide and moves between releases: a denylist would fail open on a key nobody had considered, and one such key would let an operator holding only `change_aimodel` redirect a call to a host of their choosing with the provider's credential attached.
Added the `AIModel.resolved_parameters` property, which applies the allowlist a second time and folds the resolved temperature in, so a consuming app has one dictionary to build a request from. `temperature` may be set in the column or in the parameters; the column wins, then the parameters, then the provider default, and `resolved_temperature` gives the same answer.
